 - 2026-08-21: [outer-loop] Zero-world-model induction defect fixed (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6610/6620/6630, commits 512eca0e6b + review follow-up). The 2026-08-21 supervisor A/B baseline produced 0 world models on 5 games: every induce response decoded exactly 4096 tokens (the 9B-era agent default) while the pinned Qwen3.8-27B needs 36k-83k tokens per thinking induction (median 62,490). The scored kernel pins 131072/2400 via env, so only env-less local runs failed -- silently, every time. Fix: the budget/timeout defaults are now generator-pin constants equal to the kernel's pins (parity test enforces equality), shared via one dataclass default across both live construction sites and the lever harness; per-request n_predict clamps to the running server's observed pool (llama-server admission counts prompt + n_predict); the conflated proposer_failed_or_missing_root skip label is split with the induce failure note carried onto the attempt and the harness row; induction_model_specs derives from the weights actually loaded (server /props first). Scored path byte-identical (env pins win everywhere; clamp is a no-op on the 614,400-cell scored pool and vLLM). Live acceptance re-run on the same 5 games in flight at write time; first induce call already decoded 44k+ tokens past the old cap.
